<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 558 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 558 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 558 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    700 MLN    700 MLN    700 MLN     =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    92 MLN     650 MLN     =</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    21 MLN*    494 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    71 MLN*     64 MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
